{
 "about": "RenderStutter, 2026-10-16, seed 1, AMD Radeon Pro 5500M (RDNA-1), headless Chrome at 1600x1143, each build served from its own dir and port. base: da53131 with only the bench harness added (play/main.js runs several ?bench= kinds in turn on one load and reports the worker's dearest frames with their passes and the time between finished frames; live.js keeps when each frame was finished and its passes). new: da53131 with this change. Not a quiet machine: the harness UI's GPU process (Paseo) ran at 80 to 90 percent of a core throughout, and peers' sim tests ran before 22:45; from 23:05 the operator's rule held every run under five minutes, so the after-warm benches run with ?warm=300 (the default warm takes about four minutes after the first view) and ?warm=0 was not usable (a 54 s page long task on base). Each A/B pair ran back to back. gpuMs is the GPU's span from a frame's first pass to its last (timestamps), so it takes in whatever else the GPU did meanwhile; gapMs is the time between two frames the page heard were done, what is seen.",
 "changes": {
  "tickInParts": "src/sim/sim.ts tickPause, src/gpu/store.ts beginPaced: the render worker (worker.js nextTask, a message port's task) lets the frames the page sent be drawn after the upload, after each law the GPU is given and after the ecology; the rest of the tick (life, groups, the people's turns, journeys, the landing's gather) runs in one piece as before, as the brain's promises are started from the groups on. Server, tests and scripts leave tickPause null and run as before. Identity: a seed-1 world ticked 300 ticks with and without the pause (setImmediate) gives the same events, people, things and census (sha256 12d6936561fd4787 both).",
  "mirrorWindows": "src/gpu/mirror.ts: the cells every window holds made once a landing (a mask and the cells in order) and again only when a window changes, for every kind's gather entries and every cell lookup, where each kind built a Set of them each tick. Same entries. The landing's entries were 11 ms a tick of the worker's 28 ms in the warm (profile at base).",
  "sprites": "worker.js: sprites made after the first view come from the sprite workers 16 at a time (REFRESH_CHUNK, 200 for the first view), their pixels and cast rows moved rather than copied (sprites-worker.js), and go into the atlas a part at a time between frames (PART_MS 4 ms); the page's loading line is no longer redrawn for them. At base a refresh held the worker 150 to 224 ms in one piece.",
  "asksInTick": "worker.js: a selection or window asked for while a tick is in a pause is answered with the state after the tick.",
  "sunStripes": "webgpu.js SUN_STRIPES 6 to 12: a stripe of the sun's map about 0.6 ms of a frame (1.0 to 1.4 ms measured for six).",
  "frontRows": "webgpu.js FRONT_ROWS 16 to 8: a front list's slice measured 0.3 to 5.3 ms at sixteen rows against its design's 2 ms. The list built is the same (every slice marked before any is kept).",
  "farPass": "webgpu.js: a far list's build step is timed as the pass 'far'."
 },
